explanation:
In Mathlib, `Over X` is defined as `CostructuredArrow (𝟭 T) X`, which is the comma category `Comma (𝟭 T) (Functor.fromPUnit X)`. So `CommaMorphism f g` consists of three pieces of data:
- a morphism `left : f.left ⟶ g.left` in T;
- a morphism `right` in `Discrete PUnit`, which carries no information because there is exactly one such morphism;
- the commutativity condition, which here amounts to `left ≫ g.hom = f.hom` (Mathlib proves this as the lemma `Over.w`).

These are exactly the commutative triangles over X, i.e. the morphisms of the slice category. The definition is just a named wrapper (`Over.Hom`) around the general comma-category morphism, at the natural generality of an arbitrary category T. It is faithful.
